# The design contract is a copy of a file generated in the desktop repository,
# and the only way to ask "is this still the desktop's?" is to compare the two.
# Git's autocrlf answers no on Windows even when every byte of content agrees —
# 895 line endings differ and nothing else does — which turns the one check that
# matters into a false positive, the same shape of mistake the contract itself
# was built to stop.
protocol/*.json text eol=lf
